    "label": "31",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$x+\\frac1x=\\frac9{10}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No real solutions.",
      "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $10x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}10x^2+10&=9x\\\\10x^2-9x+10&=0\\\\b^2-4ac&=(-9)^2-4(10)(10)\\\\b^2-4ac&=-319.\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic formula requires the square root of a negative number, so there are no real solutions.",
